ahezu 1.0, was zu erwarten war: PS und kW sind zwei verschiedene\nEinheiten für dieselbe physikalische Größe und über einen festen Faktor\n(1 kW = 1.35962 PS) exakt ineinander umrechenbar. Die kleine Abweichung von 1.0\nentsteht durch Rundung bei den PS-Werten im Datensatz, wie wir bereits in\nKapitel 10.1 beobachtet haben. Auch das ist ein Beispiel für hohe Korrelation\nohne Kausalfrage: Weder verursacht kW die PS-Zahl noch umgekehrt; beide\nbeschreiben dieselbe Eigenschaft.","position":{"start":{"line":254,"column":1},"end":{"line":254,"column":1}},"key":"kopnVL7XGf"}],"key":"QYeqHFGnIP"}],"class":"tip dropdown","key":"q4P5fzuhNJ"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":263,"column":1},"end":{"line":263,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regressionsgerade im Streudiagramm","position":{"start":{"line":263,"column":1},"end":{"line":263,"column":1}},"key":"Uf9nAdrTDh"}],"identifier":"regressionsgerade-im-streudiagramm","label":"Regressionsgerade im Streudiagramm","html_id":"regressionsgerade-im-streudiagramm","implicit":true,"key":"jk7FkflzGC"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":268,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bisher haben wir Regressionsgerade und Datenpunkte getrennt betrachtet. Jetzt\nzeichnen wir beides in ein gemeinsames Diagramm. Der Scatter-Plot entsteht wie\nin Kapitel 11.1 mit ","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"key":"g4g2GwOAvH"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"px.scatter()","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"key":"LrbYyueTw9"},{"type":"text","value":". Mit der Methode ","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"key":"wwLyajUVKi"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".add_scatter()","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"key":"AqJjapqiD2"},{"type":"text","value":" fügen wir\nder Abbildung eine weitere Kurve hinzu:","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"key":"FYzFFXTZM7"}],"key":"UipdSPgI7z"}],"key":"LbFblx7vJG"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport plotly.express as px\n\n# Eingabe\ndf = pd.read_csv(\"autoscout24_DE_2020_cleaned.csv\")\ndf_benzin = df[(df[\"Kraftstoff\"] == \"Benzin\") &\n               (df[\"Preis (Euro)\"] <= 100000)].dropna(subset=[\"Leistung (kW)\",\n                                                               \"Preis (Euro)\"])\n\nx = df_benzin[\"Leistung (kW)\"].values\ny = df_benzin[\"Preis (Euro)\"].values\n\n# Verarbeitung: Regression\nkoeff = np.polyfit(x, y, 1)\ngerade = np.poly1d(koeff)\nR2 = np.corrcoef(x, y)[0, 1]**2\n\nx_fit = np.linspace(x.min(), x.max(), 200)\ny_fit = gerade(x_fit)\n\n# Ausgabe: Scatter mit Regressionsgerade\nfig = px.scatter(data_frame=df_benzin,\n                 x=\"Leistung (kW)\",\n                 y=\"Preis (Euro)\",\n                 opacity=0.3,\n                 title=f\"Preis vs. Leistung (Benzin) | R² = {R2:.2f}\")\n\nfig.add_scatter(x=x_fit,\n                y=y_fit,\n                mode=\"lines\",\n                name=f\"Regression (m = {koeff[0]:.0f} €/kW)\")\nfig.show()","key":"QZ4mbgce1o"},{"type":"outputs","id":"IfJarDEDsFVGunP5xGx6U","children":[{"type":"output","children":[],"jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"894c0f0bc0c224617506b58673feec22","path":"/thma_python/build/894c0f0bc0c224617506b58673feec22.html"}}},"key":"QiCj4IpnPC"},{"type":"output","children":[],"jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"application/vnd.plotly.v1+json":{"content_type":"application/vnd.plotly.v1+json","hash":"628e7746ce82bc6b2669e91eaf95fab9","path":"/thma_python/build/628e7746ce82bc6b2669e91eaf95fab9.json"},"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"2bbbe1dcaf5bb18ba705ace07790b650","path":"/thma_python/build/2bbbe1dcaf5bb18ba705ace07790b650.html"}}},"key":"nBJcF2amGY"}],"key":"RYOfLIoNek"}],"key":"q729EC6VzK"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":306,"column":1},"end":{"line":311,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x_fit","position":{"start":{"line":306,"column":1},"end":{"line":306,"column":1}},"key":"H9vOF1KsVw"},{"type":"text","value":" ist ein gleichmäßig verteiltes Array von 200 Punkten zwischen dem\nkleinsten und größten x-Wert, erzeugt mit ","position":{"start":{"line":306,"column":1},"end":{"line":306,"column":1}},"key":"gJpCboJMP3"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"np.linspace()","position":{"start":{"line":306,"column":1},"end":{"line":306,"column":1}},"key":"H7wRsw8zNv"},{"type":"text","value":" aus Kapitel 9.1.\n","position":{"start":{"line":306,"column":1},"end":{"line":306,"column":1}},"key":"K8Pqz0zycB"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gerade(x_fit)","position":{"start":{"line":306,"column":1},"end":{"line":306,"column":1}},"key":"tsg8GqWSJb"},{"type":"text","value":" berechnet für jeden dieser Punkte den vorhergesagten Preis.\n","position":{"start":{"line":306,"column":1},"end":{"line":306,"column":1}},"key":"ATWGUWMsmZ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opacity=0.3","position":{"start":{"line":306,"column":1},"end":{"line":306,"column":1}},"key":"noFj01Z3JY"},{"type":"text","value":" macht die Datenpunkte halbtransparent, damit die Regressionsgerade\nbesser sichtbar ist. R² erscheint direkt im Titel, damit die Güte der Anpassung\nsofort ablesbar ist.","position":{"start":{"line":306,"column":1},"end":{"line":306,"column":1}},"key":"qVm9JgU0LS"}],"key":"tNBdRZzaqr"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mini-Übung","position":{"start":{"line":313,"column":1},"end":{"line":313,"column":1}},"key":"MMqUQ6uwea"}],"key":"tEbAxGtIMs"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":315,"column":1},"end":{"line":318,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Zeichnen Sie die Regressionsgerade für den Zusammenhang zwischen\n","position":{"start":{"line":315,"column":1},"end":{"line":315,"column":1}},"key":"nbFVamNOA3"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Verbrauch (l/100 km)","position":{"start":{"line":315,"column":1},"end":{"line":315,"column":1}},"key":"MGa7juEMF4"},{"type":"text","value":" und ","position":{"start":{"line":315,"column":1},"end":{"line":315,"column":1}},"key":"ZKOJZQXTi3"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Verbrauch (g/km)","position":{"start":{"line":315,"column":1},"end":{"line":315,"column":1}},"key":"YjiuEwwNB6"},{"type":"text","value":" für Benzinfahrzeuge. Verwenden\nSie die gefilterten Daten aus dem R²-Abschnitt (3 bis 20 l/100 km, 70 bis\n470 g/km). Geben Sie R² und die Steigung im Titel aus.","position":{"start":{"line":315,"column":1},"end":{"line":315,"column":1}},"key":"eJXaynNmcq"}],"key":"bDRPx8Td3h"}],"class":"tip","key":"yJb44BhlNI"}],"key":"caqwUrkgaT"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"# Code-Zelle","key":"wQ0G9jJrsN"},{"type":"outputs","id":"IdZ8WymXz3u3AOP43o0We","children":[],"key":"qrA3t3dwH1"}],"key":"RQbeu3Bpnq"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lösung","position":{"start":{"line":325,"column":1},"end":{"line":325,"column":1}},"key":"HGClwHGmw1"}],"key":"P81QMTsNMQ"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport plotly.express as px\n\n# Eingabe\ndf = pd.read_csv(\"autoscout24_DE_2020_cleaned.csv\")\ndf_v = df[(df[\"Kraftstoff\"] == \"Benzin\") &\n          (df[\"Verbrauch (l/100 km)\"] >= 3) &\n          (df[\"Verbrauch (l/100 km)\"] <= 20) &\n          (df[\"Verbrauch (g/km)\"] >= 70) &\n          (df[\"Verbrauch (g/km)\"] <= 470)].dropna(\n              subset=[\"Verbrauch (l/100 km)\", \"Verbrauch (g/km)\"])\n\nx = df_v[\"Verbrauch (l/100 km)\"].values\ny = df_v[\"Verbrauch (g/km)\"].values\n\n# Verarbeitung\nkoeff = np.polyfit(x, y, 1)\ngerade = np.poly1d(koeff)\nR2 = np.corrcoef(x, y)[0, 1]**2\n\nx_fit = np.linspace(x.min(), x.max(), 200)\ny_fit = gerade(x_fit)\n\n# Ausgabe\nfig = px.scatter(data_frame=df_v,\n                 x=\"Verbrauch (l/100 km)\",\n                 y=\"Verbrauch (g/km)\",\n                 opacity=0.2,\n                 title=f\"CO₂ vs. Kraftstoffverbrauch (Benzin) | \"\n                       f\"R² = {R2:.2f}, m = {koeff[0]:.1f} g/km pro l/100 km\")\n\nfig.add_scatter(x=x_fit,\n                y=y_fit,\n                mode=\"lines\",\n                name=\"Regression\")\nfig.show()","position":{"start":{"line":328,"column":1},"end":{"line":366,"column":1}},"key":"ZHXdTPcVLB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":368,"column":1},"end":{"line":369,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Die Regressionsgerade liegt sehr eng an den Datenpunkten. Die Steigung von etwa\n22.5 g/km pro l/100 km entspricht dem bekannten physikalischen Umrechnungsfaktor.","position":{"start":{"line":368,"column":1},"end":{"line":368,"column":1}},"key":"oBaEZzl6JL"}],"key":"GRAZK1u0kG"}],"class":"tip dropdown","key":"bc76jG4kxY"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":372,"column":1},"end":{"line":372,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Zusammenfassung und Ausblick","position":{"start":{"line":372,"column":1},"end":{"line":372,"column":1}},"key":"WukPEjN4zw"}],"identifier":"zusammenfassung-und-ausblick","label":"Zusammenfassung und Ausblick","html_id":"zusammenfassung-und-ausblick","implicit":true,"key":"HYJ5HoOaok"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":384,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In diesem Kapitel haben wir die lineare Regression als Werkzeug kennengelernt,\num Zusammenhänge in Daten zu quantifizieren. ","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":374,"column":1}},"key":"oWl82kLnCI"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"np.polyfit()","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":374,"column":1}},"key":"z78MAOzTEh"},{"type":"text","value":" berechnet Steigung\nund y-Achsenabschnitt, ","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":374,"column":1}},"key":"oX9SjFl63g"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"np.poly1d()","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":374,"column":1}},"key":"iO2CYE6YVk"},{"type":"text","value":" macht die Gerade aufrufbar, und\n","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":374,"column":1}},"key":"yWkuMqFukC"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"np.corrcoef()","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":374,"column":1}},"key":"JzQHgWyKFM"},{"type":"text","value":" liefert mit R² ein Maß für die Güte der Anpassung. Die\nVisualisierung mit ","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":374,"column":1}},"key":"B0z971XIQW"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fig.add_scatter()","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":374,"column":1}},"key":"oOw6PpN9pk"},{"type":"text","value":" verbindet die Regression mit den\nDiagrammtypen aus Kapitel 11.1. Das Verbrauch-Beispiel hat gezeigt, dass ein\nhohes R² zwar einen engen Zusammenhang anzeigt, aber keine Aussage über\nUrsache und Wirkung erlaubt. Pandas, Plotly Express und NumPy bilden zusammen\nein leistungsfähiges Werkzeugset für die Datenanalyse, das in weiterführenden\nVeranstaltungen zu maschinellem Lernen und technischer Datenanalyse ausgebaut\nwerden kann.","position":{"start":{"line":374,"column":1},"end":{"line":374,"column":1}},"key":"hB2xz60v1k"}],"key":"m8vDu0D8gq"}],"key":"X2JTA665Zd"}],"key":"Xc5Fw4eZ4H"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"11.1 Visualisierung mit DataFrames","url":"/chapter11-sec01","group":"11. Visualisierung und Regression"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}